# Design system references

Check the live documentation for component syntax, classes, spacing, typography, colours — don't rely on memory. If live browsing isn't available and something isn't covered in these rules, say so rather than stating a class name or hex value with false confidence.

- Components: <https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/>
- Patterns: <https://design-system.service.gov.uk/patterns/>
- Styles: <https://design-system.service.gov.uk/styles/>
- GOV.UK style guide: <https://www.gov.uk/guidance/style-guide/a-to-z>
- WCAG 2.2: <https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/>
- Prototype Kit docs: <https://prototype-kit.service.gov.uk/docs>

Other departments maintain their own design systems — relevant if this prototype needs to be consistent with another department's service. Full list: <https://github.com/ctdesign/gov-design-systems-list>. Includes HMRC, Home Office, DWP, Ministry of Justice, NHS, among others. Defra's own resources are in the `defra` rules.
